    "type": "question",
    "label": "26",
    "prompt": "By using $\\cos 2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1$, find the exact value of $\\cos 22.5^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos45^\\circ&=2\\cos^2 22.5^\\circ-1\\\\2\\cos^2 22.5^\\circ&=1+\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\\\\\cos^2 22.5^\\circ&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt2}{4}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $22.5^\\circ$ is in the first quadrant, $\\cos22.5^\\circ>0$.\n$$\\cos22.5^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
